WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Boundary layers. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Describe near-wall flow in words

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A boundary layer is the near-surface region where viscosity affects velocity. Surface and pressure conditions influence its development.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Velocity is near zero at the wall in the standard no-slip model and approaches the outer flow farther away.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Flow-state sorting

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Describe near-wall flow in words
